##Started building the frontend for the tool instead of accessing it through Python terminal. 
- Goal is a simple web app with form frontend. It will be hosted so it can be accessible from any device and browser 

##Building
- Decided to use Railway
- Easiest way to take a Python Flask and give it a permanent URL that I can open on any device. Also everytime the code is updated it will be pushed to GitHUb and Railway will deploy it automatically instead of me needing to download a new zip file each time. 
- The trade-off is that each file that is uploaded will only be stored temporarily on the Railway server. Which is actually better for me in terms of privacy.

##Ready
- I built the simple form frontend. It is only for my own personal use, so I kept it to the point. 
- It contains the same questions that were asked in the Python terminal, but now just in form sections. 

##Why I built the frontend
- I built it simply because using it through Python terminal was getting time-consuming. I had to apply a command everytime I wanted to use the tool, and often times I would run into tiny code issues. By applying a frontend, it doesn't require me to use any commands or codes anymore. 
